  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If \\(3x^3-9x^2+kx-12\\) is divisible by \\(x-3,\\) then it is also divisible by:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(3x^2-x+4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(3x^2-4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(3x^2+4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(3x-4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(3x+4\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1961-p22.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(P(x)=3x^3-9x^2+kx-12.\\) Since \\(x-3\\) is a factor, \\[ P(3)=81-81+3k-12=0, \\] so \\(k=4.\\) Direct division gives \\[ P(x)=(x-3)(3x^2+4). \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Apply the factor theorem at \\(x=3\\) to determine \\(k\\)",
        "Then factor out \\(x-3\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
